  </ul>
  <p class="m-0 text-[1rem] italic leading-normal text-text-primary">Lower is faster. Source: AIMultiple.</p>
</figure>

    </div></section>

    
<section class="flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-12">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:items-center lg:gap-12">
    <h2 class="max-lg:text-desktop-h4 md:max-lg:text-desktop-h3 lg:text-display-desktop-h3 lg:max-xl:text-[3.5rem] lg:order-2">No scraping. <br class="sm:max-lg:hidden">No fallback.</h2>
    <div class="lg:order-1 lg:col-span-2"><div class="text-default md:text-desktop-default [&_p+p]:pt-4 [&_a]:text-text-interactive"><p>Agents work on the long tail. With other search APIs, these long-tail queries get passed to Google or Bing.</p>
<p>Brave answers every query from its own index. No handoff. No added latency or privacy risk.</p>
</div></div>
  </div>
<figure class="card card__contents m-0 hidden flex-col gap-7 md:flex" data-theme="light">
  <figcaption class="sr-only">A long-tail query. Other search APIs fall back from their index to Google or Bing, adding latency and privacy risk. Brave answers it from its own index. Both queries are answered.</figcaption>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3.5">
    <p class="m-0 text-mobile-h4 text-text-primary sm:text-desktop-h5">Other search APIs</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <div class="shrink-0 rounded-lg border-2 border-divider-strong bg-container-background px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-primitive-neutral-30">Your agent</div>
      <div class="flex min-w-[9rem] flex-1 flex-col justify-end self-stretch">
        <span class="mb-1.5 text-center text-xs font-semibold text-primitive-neutral-30">Long-tail query</span>
