        <span class="mb-1.5 text-center text-xs font-semibold">Falls back</span>
        <span class="mb-4 block h-0.5 bg-primitive-neutral-10" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="shrink-0 rounded-lg border-2 border-primitive-neutral-10 bg-container-background px-7 py-4 font-semibold">Google or Bing</div>
      <div class="flex min-w-[13.5rem] flex-[1.5] flex-col justify-end self-stretch">
        <span class="mb-1.5 whitespace-nowrap text-center text-xs font-semibold">Latency and privacy risk</span>
        <span class="mb-4 block h-0.5 bg-primitive-neutral-10" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="shrink-0 rounded-lg border-2 border-primitive-neutral-10 bg-container-background px-8 py-4 text-center font-semibold">Answered</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="h-px bg-divider-subtle" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-3.5">
    <p class="m-0 text-mobile-h4 sm:text-desktop-h5">Brave Search API</p>
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3">
      <div class="shrink-0 rounded-lg border-2 border-divider-strong bg-container-background px-6 py-4 font-semibold text-primitive-neutral-30">Your agent</div>
      <div class="flex min-w-[9rem] flex-1 flex-col justify-end self-stretch">
        <span class="mb-1.5 text-center text-xs font-semibold text-primitive-neutral-30">Long-tail query</span>
        <span class="mb-4 block h-0.5 bg-divider-strong" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="shrink-0 rounded-lg bg-primitive-brands-rorange-1 px-8 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Brave's own index</div>
      <div class="flex min-w-[12rem] flex-1 flex-col justify-end self-stretch">
        <span class="mb-1.5 whitespace-nowrap text-center text-xs font-semibold text-primitive-brands-rorange-1">Same infrastructure</span>
        <span class="mb-4 block h-0.5 bg-primitive-brands-rorange-1" aria-hidden="true"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="shrink-0 rounded-lg bg-primitive-brands-rorange-1 px-8 py-4 font-semibold text-white">Answered</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</figure>
</section>

    
<section class="flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-12">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:items-center lg:gap-12">
    <h2 class="max-lg:text-desktop-h4 md:max-lg:text-desktop-h3 lg:text-display-desktop-h3 lg:max-xl:text-[3.5rem] lg:order-2">Access that can’t be shut down</h2>
    <div class="lg:order-1 lg:col-span-2"><div class="text-default md:text-desktop-default [&_p+p]:pt-4 [&_a]:text-text-interactive"><p>Microsoft retired the Bing Search APIs. Google closed Custom Search API to new customers. Now they’re taking action against scrapers.</p>
<p>Brave doesn’t have this exposure. Our index is our own: crawled, ranked, and served end to end.</p>
</div></div>
  </div></section>

  </div>

  
<section class="mt-10 lg:mt-16 flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-12">
  <div>
    <h2 class="max-lg:text-desktop-h4 md:max-lg:text-desktop-h3 lg:text-display-desktop-h4">Super low CPMs have hidden costs</h2><div class="pt-4 text-default md:text-desktop-default [&_p+p]:pt-4 [&_a]:text-text-interactive"><p>List prices only tell half the story. True cost is total search + tokens per correct answer.</p>
<p>Brave serves better data on the first call. Fewer tokens, lower inference costs, and more room for more sources in every call.</p>
</div></div>
<figure class="m-0 flex flex-col gap-4 rounded-xl bg-neutral-10 p-6 md:p-7" data-theme="light">
