<section class="mt-10 md:mt-20"><ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3"><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Cheapest per correct answer</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">In FreshQA, Brave scored 85.3% accuracy at $18 per 1,000 questions (vs. $49 - $89 for competitors).</div></li><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Only what your model needs</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">LLM Context returns only the content your model needs to answer the question. Ranked. Extracted. Compact.</div></li><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Prepaid credits, no subscription</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Load credits, use as you go. Set your own token budget. No minimums, no surprise bills.</div></li></ul>
</section>

  
<section class="mt-10 lg:mt-16 flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-12">
  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3 lg:items-center lg:gap-12">
    <h2 class="max-lg:text-desktop-h4 md:max-lg:text-desktop-h3 lg:text-display-desktop-h3 lg:max-xl:text-[3.5rem] lg:order-2">99.9% of the web that matters</h2>
    <div class="lg:order-1 lg:col-span-2"><div class="text-default md:text-desktop-default [&_p+p]:pt-4 [&_a]:text-text-interactive"><p>Index size is a vanity stat. For agents, it’s page quality that matters.</p>
<p>Brave’s index is built by anonymous contributions from real browser &amp; search users (and their agents). Every day, millions of signals on the real content that’s really useful.</p>
<p>That means less SEO spam, less AI slop, and more of the web that matters.</p>
</div></div>
  </div></section>

  
<section class="mt-10 md:mt-20 mb-10 lg:mb-16"><h2 class="text-display-mobile-h1 sm:text-display-h3 mb-10">Control you won’t find anywhere else</h2><ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-3"><li class="card card__contents"><span class="icon mb-2 block [--icon-size:2rem] [--icon-url:url(/leo-icons/search-goggles.svg)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Goggles</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Re-rank results. Define custom domain sets. <a href="https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/documentation/resources/goggles" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Learn more.</a></div></li><li class="card card__contents"><span class="icon mb-2 block [--icon-size:2rem] [--icon-url:url(/leo-icons/article.svg)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Extra snippets</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Up to five more per result. Richer context.</div></li><li class="card card__contents"><span class="icon mb-2 block [--icon-size:2rem] [--icon-url:url(/leo-icons/hierarchy-structure.svg)]" aria-hidden="true"></span><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Schema-enriched results</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Structured data. Any format. Ready to use.</div></li></ul>
</section>


  <div class="layout gap-y-10 bg-neutral-10 py-10 lg:gap-y-16 lg:py-16">
    
<section class="flex flex-col gap-8 lg:gap-12">
  <div>
    <h2 class="max-lg:text-desktop-h4 md:max-lg:text-desktop-h3 lg:text-display-desktop-h4">Search results are for people. Brave’s LLM Context endpoint is for machines.</h2><div class="pt-4 text-default md:text-desktop-default [&_p+p]:pt-4 [&_a]:text-text-interactive"><p>A results page gives titles and snippets. Agents need parsed data, pre-formatted and pre-filtered for answers.</p>
<p>Brave’s LLM Context delivers just that: The best passages from the best pages, ranked in a single call.</p>
</div></div></section>

    
<section><ul class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Every kind of content</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Text. Tables. Code. JSON. Forum threads. Video captions.</div></li><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Configure your search</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Set from 1k to ~33k tokens. Get just the context you need.</div></li><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Only what&#39;s relevant</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Pick a threshold: strict, balanced, or lenient. Noise stays out.</div></li><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Fresh and traceable</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Every source carries URL &amp; timestamp. Filter to the last 24 hours, and get metadata to see last fetch.</div></li><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Your sources, your rules</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Use Goggles to choose which sites ground your model.</div></li><li><h3 class="mb-2 sm:text-desktop-h4">Local, too</h3>
          <div class="[&_a]:text-text-interactive [&_p+p]:pt-4">Location-aware results, with places and map data.</div></li></ul>
</section>
<section data-tab-group class="mt-0">
