  <section id="faq" class="mt-16 md:mt-20">
    <h2 class="text-desktop-h4 md:text-desktop-h3 pb-8">
      FAQs
    </h2>
    
<details class="card card__contents group px-8 py-0 border-divider-strong [&:not(:first-child)]:-mt-[--card-contents-border-width] [&:not(:first-of-type)]:rounded-t-none [&:not(:last-of-type)]:rounded-b-none overflow-hidden">
    <summary class="text-blockquote [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden [-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent] list-none flex gap-2 items-start py-6 cursor-pointer" data-accordion-heading>
        Does Brave ever use Google or Bing results?
        <span class="icon [--icon-url:url(/static-assets/icons/arrow-alt-down.svg)] flex-shrink-0 ms-auto transition-transform duration-100 mt-[0.2rem] group-open:rotate-180"></span>
    </summary>
    <div class="-mt-2 pb-6 prose" data-accordion-content>
        
  










<p>No. Every result comes from Brave&rsquo;s own independent index, crawled and ranked by Brave. There is no fallback to another search engine for any query.</p>


    </div>
</details>

<details class="card card__contents group px-8 py-0 border-divider-strong [&:not(:first-child)]:-mt-[--card-contents-border-width] [&:not(:first-of-type)]:rounded-t-none [&:not(:last-of-type)]:rounded-b-none overflow-hidden">
    <summary class="text-blockquote [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden [-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent] list-none flex gap-2 items-start py-6 cursor-pointer" data-accordion-heading>
        Why do you ask for a credit card?
        <span class="icon [--icon-url:url(/static-assets/icons/arrow-alt-down.svg)] flex-shrink-0 ms-auto transition-transform duration-100 mt-[0.2rem] group-open:rotate-180"></span>
    </summary>
    <div class="-mt-2 pb-6 prose" data-accordion-content>
        









<p>To prevent abuse. Brave uses prepaid credits, not subscriptions, so you&rsquo;re only charged for credits you choose to buy.</p>


    </div>
</details>

<details class="card card__contents group px-8 py-0 border-divider-strong [&:not(:first-child)]:-mt-[--card-contents-border-width] [&:not(:first-of-type)]:rounded-t-none [&:not(:last-of-type)]:rounded-b-none overflow-hidden">
    <summary class="text-blockquote [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden [-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent] list-none flex gap-2 items-start py-6 cursor-pointer" data-accordion-heading>
        How is Brave&rsquo;s Zero Data Retention different?
        <span class="icon [--icon-url:url(/static-assets/icons/arrow-alt-down.svg)] flex-shrink-0 ms-auto transition-transform duration-100 mt-[0.2rem] group-open:rotate-180"></span>
    </summary>
    <div class="-mt-2 pb-6 prose" data-accordion-content>
        









<p>Most ZDR is a contractual promise that can only cover queries the vendor answers itself. Brave&rsquo;s ZDR is architectural: every query ends on infrastructure we operate end to end, so there&rsquo;s no third party to retain it.</p>


    </div>
</details>

<details class="card card__contents group px-8 py-0 border-divider-strong [&:not(:first-child)]:-mt-[--card-contents-border-width] [&:not(:first-of-type)]:rounded-t-none [&:not(:last-of-type)]:rounded-b-none overflow-hidden">
    <summary class="text-blockquote [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden [-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent] list-none flex gap-2 items-start py-6 cursor-pointer" data-accordion-heading>
        Can I store results or use them to train models?
        <span class="icon [--icon-url:url(/static-assets/icons/arrow-alt-down.svg)] flex-shrink-0 ms-auto transition-transform duration-100 mt-[0.2rem] group-open:rotate-180"></span>
    </summary>
    <div class="-mt-2 pb-6 prose" data-accordion-content>
        









<p>Yes, with a <a href="https://api-dashboard.search.brave.com/documentation/pricing" target="_blank" rel="noopener">plan</a> that includes storage rights.</p>


    </div>
</details>

<details class="card card__contents group px-8 py-0 border-divider-strong [&:not(:first-child)]:-mt-[--card-contents-border-width] [&:not(:first-of-type)]:rounded-t-none [&:not(:last-of-type)]:rounded-b-none overflow-hidden">
    <summary class="text-blockquote [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden [-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent] list-none flex gap-2 items-start py-6 cursor-pointer" data-accordion-heading>
        Where does Brave&rsquo;s data come from?
        <span class="icon [--icon-url:url(/static-assets/icons/arrow-alt-down.svg)] flex-shrink-0 ms-auto transition-transform duration-100 mt-[0.2rem] group-open:rotate-180"></span>
    </summary>
    <div class="-mt-2 pb-6 prose" data-accordion-content>
        









<p>Brave&rsquo;s own web crawler, plus privacy-preserving signals from Brave users who opt in to the <a href="https://support.brave.app/hc/en-us/articles/4409406835469-What-is-the-Web-Discovery-Project" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Web Discovery Project</a>. Its code is open source, so anyone can audit it.</p>


    </div>
</details>

  </section>

