      </article><article class="card card__contents mt-10 mb-10 lg:mt-16 lg:mb-16">
    <div class="article mx-auto w-full max-w-[var(--article-width)]">
      <h2>
        The Brave Search API story
      </h2><h3>
          Answer quality <em>is</em> index quality
        </h3><p>To generate great answers, agents need machine-readable data from a global-scale, real-time index of the Web. Google and Bing have shut down their services; needle tests prove all other services scrape (even those claiming not to). This violates Google’s ToS, and returns low-quality, token-inefficient data built for humans. Blue links can’t train AI; scraping is too risky for critical infrastructure like Web search.</p>
<p>Brave is the only fully-fledged search index available through an open API, and it’s the only index built by signals from 130+ million real humans. These anonymous clicks and queries (via Brave browser and Brave Search) help combat AI slop and SEO spam. Indexing 99.9% of the web that matters, Brave has the data agents need, how and when they need it.</p>
<p>Brave’s LLM Context API returns pre-extracted, relevance-scored content chunks (text, tables, code) optimized for machine consumption, eliminating the need for separate scraping and parsing steps. This data-first approach reduces latency to under 500ms at P90, cuts token usage by up to 4x, and provides higher-quality grounding data that helps agents generate more accurate responses with fewer hallucinations on fewer calls.</p>
<p>Brave offers low CPM, high throughput, and high uptime. Structural ZDR vs contractual. SOC2 Type II attestation and regular security audits. Endpoints across LLM grounding (agent search); web search for humans; news, images, video, and places; and even pre-built answers. 3rd-party verified as having the highest agent quality and lowest latency of any provider, Brave is the choice to power your AI.</p>
</div>
  </article>

